This code uses Moore's Voting Algorithm to find the majority element in a given array. It iterates through the array once and maintains a candidate for the majority element. Then it validates this candidate by counting its occurrences in the array again, returning it if more than n/2 elements match, otherwise returning -1.

Note: This code assumes that there is at least one majority element present in the given array. If there might be no majority element, you should return a special value to indicate this or handle it according to your specific requirements.

